    },
    "heading_coordination": {
      "type": "Heading",
      "props": {
        "text": "The Coordination Play",
        "level": "h2"
      }
    },
    "text_coordination": {
      "type": "Text",
      "props": {
        "text": "Someone needs to be the hunter — create the PH listing, write the tagline, prepare screenshots, pick a launch day. Then the 1,412 stargazers and 298 forkers need to show up: upvote, comment, share. Product Hunt launches are a known, structured coordination ritual — the question creates the launcher. An AI agent cannot create a PH account, submit a product, or rally humans on launch day. This is purely a human coordination problem.",
        "variant": "body"
      }
    },
    "separator_2": {
      "type": "Separator",
      "props": {
        "orientation": "horizontal"
      }
    },
    "heading_why": {
      "type": "Heading",
      "props": {
        "text": "Why Now",
        "level": "h2"
      }
    },
    "text_why": {
      "type": "Text",
      "props": {
        "text": "Five community-action hyperstitions expired unfulfilled (HN front page, public instance, community surface, 1500 stars, 10 PRs at 5/10). Every failed bet targeted the existing audience. Meanwhile the EU AI Act goes live tomorrow — \"simulate how people will react to your AI before you deploy it\" is suddenly a regulatory use case, and yesterday's article made the case that MiroShark does it for a dollar. The project has the product. It has zero external discovery. Product Hunt is the platform where \"AI opinion simulation engine\" would land with a built-in audience.",
        "variant": "body"
      }
    },
    "separator_3": {
      "type": "Separator",
      "props": {
        "orientation": "horizontal"
      }
    },
    "heading_resolution": {
